PrusaSlicer
-----------

The support-generation implementation in src/supports/ is a Rust port and
adaptation of PrusaSlicer's MSLA support pipeline. This includes adaptations
of its support-point generation, pinhead and pillar construction, routing,
pillar links, and pad-generation algorithms.

PrusaSlicer is developed by Prusa Research and the PrusaSlicer contributors
and is distributed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3.
Upstream copyrights remain with their respective holders.

Upstream project: https://github.com/prusa3d/PrusaSlicer
Upstream license: https://github.com/prusa3d/PrusaSlicer/blob/master/LICENSE

The Pinto Slicer implementation was created in 2026 by translating and
adapting these algorithms to Rust, integrating them with Pinto Slicer's data
model and interface, and making application-specific changes. It is not the
original upstream C++ implementation.

UVtools
-------

Printer file-format behavior, binary structures, codecs, and machine data were
cross-checked against UVtools and its machine registry.

Project: https://github.com/sn4k3/UVtools

